kground-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> SCIP </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> <a href=\"https://www.scipopt.org/\"><code>scip</code></a> </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> XPRESS* </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> <a href=\"https://www.fico.com/en/products/fico-xpress-optimization\"><code>xpress</code></a> </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;background-color: rgba(236, 236, 236, 1) !important;\"> ✓ </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n<tfoot>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 0; \" colspan=\"100%\">\n<sup></sup> * Commercial solver; free academic licenses are available.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 0; \" colspan=\"100%\">\n<sup></sup> QP: solvers with a quadratic-objective interface receive the objective directly; the other conic solvers solve a second-order-cone reformulation.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 0; \" colspan=\"100%\">\n<sup></sup> Without a commercial solver, mixed-integer problems can use HIGHS or GLPK_MI (MILP only), SCIP (MILP, MIQP, MISOCP) or ECOS_BB.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 0; \" colspan=\"100%\">\n<sup></sup> ECOS_BB is used only when named, as in psolve(prob, solver = \"ECOS_BB\").</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 0; \" colspan=\"100%\">\n<sup></sup> Smooth nonlinear programs, psolve(prob, nlp = TRUE), use the separate NLP solvers Uno or IPOPT; see Using Other Solvers.</td></tr>\n</tfoot>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Installing Commercial Solvers\n\n### MOSEK\n\n[MOSEK](https://www.mosek.com) provides an academic version that is\nfree of charge: one can obtain the free academic license after\nregistering. Once the license for the product has been activated, the\n[Rmosek documentation](https://docs.mosek.com/latest/rmosek/index.html)\nprovides all the details for installation. A quick check to ensure\nthings are working is to run the example:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(Rmosek)\nexample(mosek)\n```\n:::\n\n\n### Gurobi\n\n[Gurobi](https://www.gurobi.com/) offers free academic licenses. After\ninstalling Gurobi and the `gurobi` R package (bundled with the Gurobi\ninstallation), verify with:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(gurobi)\nmodel <- list(A = matrix(c(1, 1), nrow = 1),\n              obj = c(1, 1), sense = \"<=\", rhs = 1)\ngurobi(model)\n```\n:::\n\n\n### CPLEX\n\n[IBM CPLEX](https://www.ibm.com/products/ilog-cplex-optimization-studio)\nis available through IBM's academic initiative. Install the `Rcplex`\npackage from CRAN after installing the CPLEX library.\n\nOnce a commercial solver is installed, you can use it by passing\n`solver = \"MOSEK\"`, `solver = \"GUROBI\"`, or `solver = \"CPLEX\"` to\n`psolve()`.\n\n## Session Info\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\nR version 4.6.1 (2026-06-24)\nPlatform: aarch64-apple-darwin23\nRunning under: macOS Tahoe 26.6.2\n\nMatrix products: default\nBLAS:   /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.6/Resources/lib/libRblas.0.dylib \nLAPACK: /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.6/Resources/lib/libRlapack.dylib;  LAPACK version 3.12.1\n\nlocale:\n[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8\n\ntime zone: America/Los_Angeles\ntzcode source: internal\n\nattached base packages:\n[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     \n\nother a